 "text": "Hi! How's life treating you? Pack them in coolers with ice packs or a frozen bag in the fridge. Frozen water bottles work if you' out of room. Keep it in a cool, dark spot with a neck pillow so the sun doesn't warm it up. A bit, but it' worth a try. A white bottle in sun can heat up quite a lot, so a dark one stays cooler. Make sure they' in a cooler with ice, not just in the fridge. The fridge heat makes them sweat, and sweating is the last thing you want at a picnic.",
